MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The whole page (header, all 6 tab active-states, activity stat cards,
profile completion, help box, download/delete sections) used raw
indigo/purple/pink/emerald/teal/cyan/violet/rose/blue Tailwind
colors with no connection to the coral/ocean/navy brand palette —
looked like it belonged to a different app.

- Header + activity stat cards: brand (coral), accent (ocean), and
  navy, matching the site's actual palette.
- The 6 profile tabs previously each had a different rainbow
  gradient for their active state; simplified to one consistent
  brand treatment since the icon + label already distinguish them —
  matches how active states work elsewhere in the app (nav links use
  a single active color, not one per item).
- Profile completion, "How This Helps You", and the trip status
  controls box: ocean/accent tokens instead of raw blue/indigo.
- Delete Account section: switched from raw red-* to the actual
  `danger`/`danger-hover` design tokens.
- Left the Quick Trip badge's orange alone — that's the established,
  consistent color for Quick Trip UI elsewhere in the app, not a
  rebrand miss.

